Error [E0119]: There's no type called `NoClone`
  --> move_non_clonable_is_hard_error.jet:2:19
    |
  2 | fn consume(item: ^NoClone) {
    |                   ^^^^^^^
 Why: The types are `Int`, `Float`, `Bool`, and `String` (plus types you define)
 Fix: Check the spelling, or define the struct or enum first
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0119

Error [E0112]: `consume` wants `NoClone` for argument 1, but this is String (text)
  --> move_non_clonable_is_hard_error.jet:8:13
    |
  8 |     consume(msg)
    |             ^^^
 Why: Every argument must match its parameter's type
 Fix: Use `NoClone` here
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0112

Error [E0201]: `consume` needs the move marker `^` here — this value can't be copied
  --> move_non_clonable_is_hard_error.jet:8:13
    |
  8 |     consume(msg)
    |             ^^^
 Why: Parameter 1 takes ownership through the move marker `^`; passing `msg` without that marker would have to copy it, but this type can't be copied
 Fix: Write the move marker `^` (`^msg`) to move ownership to `consume`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0201
